The '''Quelii sector'''<ref name="Dawn">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref> was a [[sector]]<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> of the [[Outer Rim Territories]] region of [[the galaxy]]. It contained the [[Dathomir system]],<ref name="Appendix" /> where a [[Battle of Dathomir|battle]] was fought between the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and the [[Nightsisters]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Massacre" />

{{Sec-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Quelii sector, albeit unidentified, appeared in "[[Nightsisters (episode)|Nightsisters]]," the twelfth episode of the animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season Three|third season]],<ref name="Nightsisters">{{TCW|Nightsisters (episode)}}</ref> which aired on [[January 7]], [[2011]].<ref name="Nightsisters EG">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode312.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Nightsisters}}</ref> The sector was later identified in the [[2015]] [[Dorling Kindersley]] reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]'', though it was misspelled as "Quelli."<ref name="USW" /> Other sources, such as the [[Fantasy Flight Games]] sourcebook ''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]'', had since corrected the spelling to "Quelii."<ref name="Dawn" />

In the [[2024]] Dorling Kindersley reference book ''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]'', the [[planet]] [[Abafar]] was moved to the Quelii sector<ref name="CGSWG">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> its previous placement in the [[Sprizen sector]].<ref name="UltimateSW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> The Abafar system was also moved to the Quelii sector in "[[Star Systems of the Galaxy]]," a canon appendix published alongside the [[Star Wars Galaxy Map|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map]] on [[StarWars.com]]<ref name="Appendix" /> on [[June 24]], [[2025]],<ref name="Substack">{{Substack|subdomain=jasonfry|url=p/about-that-new-star-wars-galaxy-map|text=About That New Star Wars Galaxy Map&hellip;|name=[[Jason Fry]]|username=jasonfry|date=2025-06-24}}</ref> further supporting the change.<ref name="Appendix" /> [[Jason Fry]]&mdash;an author who contributed on the appendix<ref name="Substack" />&mdash;stated that there were no plans of changing the [[star system]]'s current placement when asked.<ref name="Email">{{EmailCite|email=File:GalaxyMapAppendix-JasonFryEmail.png|creator=[[Jason Fry]]|date=2025-06-30}}</ref>

